source	Plato, Republic I 349b-350c, tr. B. Jowett
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 1497, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/1497
class	equivocation
word	more
fault	"to desire more than" (pleonektein) is to try to get the better of another, to take a larger share, in the just and unjust man; and to try to go beyond another's performance of an art, in the musician and physician: the likeness of the just to the wise holds only on one sense throughout
reference	J. Annas, An Introduction to Plato's Republic (1981), ch. 2; R. C. Cross and A. D. Woozley, Plato's Republic (1964), ch. 2
